<section class="hero" id="top"><div class="wrap two">
 <div>
  <p class="stage"><span class="chip sm off">Pre-revenue · no outside users yet · solo founder, self-funded</span></p>
  <h1>Your whole health, read together. An agent that acts on it.</h1>
  <p class="lead">VitaCrypt reads DNA, labs, wearables, microbiome, check-ins and the air you breathe as one profile, checks every link against research, and its Lab Agent turns it into a plan that it follows up.</p>
  <div class="cta"><a class="btn p big" href="mailto:investors@vitacrypt.xyz?subject=VitaCrypt%20call%20with%20the%20founder">Talk to the founder<small>investors@vitacrypt.xyz</small></a><a class="tb" href="https://app.vitacrypt.xyz/demo">Try the live demo</a><a class="tb" href="/agent#demo">Watch the demo · 3 min</a></div>
  <nav class="jump" aria-label="Jump to section"><a class="tb" href="#thesis">Opportunity</a><a class="tb" href="#why">Why now</a><a class="tb" href="#moat">Where we lead</a><a class="tb" href="#traction">The numbers</a><a class="tb" href="#founder">Founder</a><a class="tb" href="#raise">The plan</a></nav>
 </div>
 <div>
  <ul class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
   <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8"/></svg></span><div><h3>Tap to run</h3><p>You start each run. Every outside action waits for a tap.</p></div></li><li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="6" width="16" height="12" rx="3"/><path d="M8 12l2.500 2.500L16 9.500"/></svg></span><div><h3>Cited, Hypothesis or Ask your clinician</h3><p>Each plan item is marked. No diagnoses.</p></div></li><li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="5" width="16" height="15" rx="3"/><path d="M4 10h16M9 3v4M15 3v4"/></svg></span><div><h3>Dated retest</h3><p>Set with the plan.</p></div></li><li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12l4 4 10-10"/></svg></span><div><h3>Grades its own plan</h3><p>Checked at the next lab.</p></div></li>
  </ul>
  <details><summary>The Lab Agent in full</summary><div><p>The Lab Agent is the product. You tap to run a new lab; it returns a plan where each item is marked Cited, Hypothesis or Ask your clinician, sets a dated retest, and at the next lab checks whether the plan worked. Every outside action waits for a tap, and it never diagnoses. Pre-revenue, no outside users yet, and we say so.</p></div></details>
 </div>
</div></section>

<section id="thesis"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>Your health lives in a dozen apps. The patterns live between them.</h2>
 <p class="lead">DNA in one report, labs in a PDF, sleep in a watch app, and the air you breathe in none of them.</p>
 <ol class="grid g3">
  <li class="tile"><div style="display:flex;gap:12px"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="3" width="8" height="8" rx="2"/><rect x="13" y="13" width="8" height="8" rx="2"/><path d="M15 5h6M3 17h6"/></svg></span><div><h3>Fragments</h3><p class="small">Health AI mostly reads one source.</p></div></div></li><li class="tile"><div style="display:flex;gap:12px"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 20V10M10 20V4M16 20v-7M22 20H2"/></svg></span><div><h3>Dashboards without follow up</h3><p class="small">Nobody checks later.</p></div></div></li><li class="tile"><div style="display:flex;gap:12px"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l8 3v6c0 4.500-3.300 7.800-8 9-4.700-1.200-8-4.500-8-9V6z"/></svg></span><div><h3>Trust</h3><p class="small">Advice mixes studies with guesses and sales.</p></div></div></li>
 </ol>
 <h3 style="margin-top:32px">Three buyers who already pay for their own health data</h3>
 <ul class="grid g3">
  <li class="tile"><span class="chip sm off">The optimizer</span><p class="small" style="margin-top:10px">Wears a ring daily, tests blood a few times a year.</p></li>
  <li class="tile"><span class="chip sm off">The targeted preventer</span><p class="small" style="margin-top:10px">Came in through family history.</p></li>
  <li class="tile"><span class="chip sm off">The privacy holdout</span><p class="small" style="margin-top:10px">Refuses to centralize genome and bloodwork.</p></li>
 </ul>
 <h3 style="margin-top:32px">Market, bottom-up, at USD 199 a year</h3>
 <ul class="fun">
  <li class="stat"><b>~42M</b><span>TAM: people who hold consumer DNA results</span><small>USD 8.4B a year</small></li><li class="stat"><b>~19M</b><span>SAM: those who also own a wearable</span><small>USD 3.8B a year</small></li><li class="stat"><b>100</b><span>SOM: founding members, sized by onboarding capacity</span><small>USD 20K a year</small></li>
 </ul>
 <p class="cap">The price is a plan, not charged yet.</p>
 <details><summary>Buyers in full, sizing logic and sources</summary><div>
  <p><b>The optimizer.</b> Wears a ring or band daily, has a DNA kit, tests blood a few times a year, has tried to join it all in a spreadsheet. Buys the whole-profile reading.</p>
  <p><b>The targeted preventer.</b> Came in through family history, such as a parent's early heart event. Fewer gadgets, higher willingness to pay. Buys genetics and labs read together, and the dated retest.</p>
  <p><b>The privacy holdout.</b> Refuses to centralize genome and bloodwork after the 23andMe breach. We tell them exactly what our server can do today; client-held keys are roadmap.</p>
  <p><b>Fragments.</b> Health AI today mostly reads one source and explains it. It does not read the whole person.</p>
  <p><b>Dashboards without follow up.</b> Nobody follows up. The Lab Agent sets a dated retest and grades its own plan on the next lab.</p>
  <p><b>Trust.</b> Advice mixes studies with guesses and sales. The 2023 23andMe breach affected about 6.9 million people. Every link we draw is labelled Cited, with PMIDs, or Hypothesis.</p>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Who</th><th>At USD 199 a year</th></tr></thead><tbody>
   <tr><td>TAM, about 42M people</td><td>Hold consumer DNA results: Ancestry over 29M, 23andMe over 13M (overlap not removed)</td><td>About USD 8.4B a year</td></tr>
   <tr><td>SAM, about 19M</td><td>The 46% of them who also own a wearable (Rock Health 2025, US adults, used as a proxy)</td><td>About USD 3.8B a year</td></tr>
   <tr><td>SOM, 100 founding members</td><td>First paying cohort, sized by onboarding capacity: 7 to 9 personal onboardings a week for about 13 weeks</td><td>About USD 20K a year</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <p>Price is a plan, not charged yet. Sources: Ancestry 2025 Impact Report; 23andMe testimony to the US Senate, 11 Jun 2025; Rock Health 2025. Common spine: 30 to 50, mostly US, already spends on own health, data-literate.</p>
 </div></details>
 <p class="cta" style="margin-top:12px"><a class="tb" href="/agent">How the Lab Agent works</a><a class="tb" href="/platform.html">See the platform</a></p>
</div></section>

<section id="why"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>People already pay for their health data, and now they ask AI about it.</h2>
 <p class="lead">Consumers buy DNA kits, wearables and lab panels, and a growing share asks a chatbot what the results mean.</p>
 <ul class="stats">
  <li class="stat"><b>32%</b><span>of US adults used an AI chatbot for health in 2025</span><small>Rock Health, double 2024</small></li><li class="stat"><b>$2.5B</b><span>Function Health valuation at its $298M Series B</span><small><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2025/11/19/function-health-closes-298m-series-b-at-a-2-5b-valuation-launches-medical-intelligence" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TechCrunch, 19 Nov 2025</a></small></li><li class="stat"><b>$30M</b><span>Superpower Series A</span><small>Apr 2025, over $300M post</small></li><li class="stat"><b>6.9M</b><span>people hit by the 23andMe breach</span><small>2023, then settlements and a bankruptcy sale in 2025</small></li>
 </ul>
 <p class="cap"><a class="tb" href="/platform.html">How every citation is checked</a></p>
 <details><summary>What is missing, and the citation guarantee</summary><div>
  <p>Function Health ran over 50 million lab tests since 2023. What is missing is an agent that reads all of it together, cites its sources and comes back at the next lab.</p>
  <p>Invented citations: every PMID is checked and invented PMIDs are stripped by design, with tests in CI. The plan says Hypothesis when the science is not there.</p>
 </div></details>
</div></section>

<section id="moat"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>Others see one source. VitaCrypt reads the whole person, and follows up.</h2>
 <p class="lead">We lead on local air read with DNA and labs, and on the retest loop. Others lead on reach, devices and capital.</p>
 <ul class="mx">
  <li><h3>Reads the whole person</h3><div class="cmp"><div><span class="mono">VitaCrypt</span><p class="us">Six kinds of data in one plan. In the products we reviewed, none links local air with genotype.</p><div class="chips"><span class="chip sm on-lab"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 3h6M10 3v11l-3.500 5a1.500 1.500 0 0 0 1.300 2.300h8.400a1.500 1.500 0 0 0 1.300-2.300L14 14V3"/></svg>Labs</span><span class="chip sm on-dna"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 3c0 5 10 5 10 9s-10 4-10 9M17 3c0 5-10 5-10 9s10 4 10 9M9 7h6M9 17h6"/></svg>DNA</span><span class="chip sm on-gut"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="9" cy="10" r="5"/><circle cx="17.500" cy="7.500" r="2.500"/><circle cx="16" cy="16.500" r="3.500"/></svg>Gut</span><span class="chip sm on-wear"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="6" y="7" width="12" height="10" rx="3"/><path d="M9 7l.500-4h5l.500 4M9 17l.500 4h5l.500-4"/></svg>Wearable</span><span class="chip sm on-chk"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8.500 14.500c1 1.200 2.200 1.800 3.500 1.800s2.500-.600 3.500-1.800M9 9.800v.400M15 9.800v.400"/></svg>Check-ins</span><span class="chip sm on-air"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><path d="M12 3v2M12 19v2M3 12h2M19 12h2M5.600 5.600l1.400 1.400M17 17l1.400 1.400M5.600 18.400L7 17M17 7l1.400-1.400"/></svg>Air &amp; UV</span></div></div><div><span class="mono">Most apps we reviewed</span><p>Mostly one source.</p></div></div></li>
  <li><h3>Follows up</h3><div class="cmp"><div><span class="mono">VitaCrypt</span><p class="us">A dated retest, then it grades its own plan: keep, swap or retire each habit.</p></div><div><span class="mono">Most apps we reviewed</span><p>Mostly dashboards.</p></div></div></li>
  <li><h3>Says how sure it is</h3><div class="cmp"><div><span class="mono">VitaCrypt</span><p class="us"><span class="ev c">Cited</span><span class="ev h">Hypothesis</span><span class="ev a">Ask your clinician</span><br>Checked against PubMed and Europe PMC.</p></div><div><span class="mono">Most apps we reviewed</span><p>Not compared in detail.</p></div></div></li>
  <li><h3>Acts, after a tap</h3><div class="cmp"><div><span class="mono">VitaCrypt</span><p class="us">Reminders, a clinician link, labs nearby, a lab order (US sandbox).</p></div><div><span class="mono">Most apps we reviewed</span><p>Not compared in detail.</p></div></div></li>
 </ul>
 <p class="note"><b>Who is ahead of us.</b> ChatGPT Health on reach; Function Health on capital and its own lab panels (<a href="https://techcrunch.com/2025/11/19/function-health-closes-298m-series-b-at-a-2-5b-valuation-launches-medical-intelligence" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TechCrunch, 19 Nov 2025</a>); VitaDAO's Vita App on device connections and user-held keys. Public pages and our own review, Nov 2026.</p>
 <h3 style="margin-top:32px">Safety, as built</h3>
 <ul class="grid g3">
  <li class="tile"><div style="display:flex;gap:12px"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="11" width="14" height="9" rx="2"/><path d="M8 11V8a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3"/></svg></span><div><h3>Fixed agent</h3><p class="small">Seven fixed steps. A guard blocks doses and diagnoses.</p></div></div></li><li class="tile"><div style="display:flex;gap:12px"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h12M12 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span><div><h3>What leaves</h3><p class="small">The Lab Agent's seven steps send coded facts only. Lab reading and older insight cards send more.</p></div></div></li><li class="tile"><div style="display:flex;gap:12px"><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v6M12 16.500v.500"/></svg></span><div><h3>Limits we state</h3><p class="small">Our server can unwrap your key. Zero data retention is requested, not confirmed.</p></div></div></li>
 </ul>
 <p class="cta"><a class="tb" href="/data">What happens to your data</a></p>
 <details><summary>Safety by construction, in full</summary><div>
  <p><b>Fixed agent.</b> Seven fixed steps and a fixed tool list in code. Fixed rules decide what the agent does; the model judges papers and words the plan. An output guard blocks doses, medication changes and diagnoses.</p>
  <p><b>What leaves.</b> The Lab Agent's seven steps send coded fields only to the model (Anthropic's Claude): the Lab Agent never receives a name, email, file or exact value. Searches carry gene and marker names only. Every send is logged in the app. Lab reading is a separate call: the report text goes to Claude with lines that identify the person removed, and the removal can miss an unlabelled name. Older insight cards send a fuller profile.</p>
  <p><b>Who is ahead of us, in full.</b> ChatGPT Health on reach; Function Health on capital and its own lab panels, valued at $2.5B after a $298M Series B (<a href="https://techcrunch.com/2025/11/19/function-health-closes-298m-series-b-at-a-2-5b-valuation-launches-medical-intelligence" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TechCrunch, 19 Nov 2025</a>); VitaDAO's Vita App on device connections, open sign-up and self-reported user-held keys. Based on public pages and our own review, Nov 2026.</p>
  <p><b>Cited or Hypothesis.</b> Every link is checked against PubMed and Europe PMC by an AI judge; no invented PMIDs. Clinical topics become questions for your clinician.</p>
  <p><b>Acts, after a tap.</b> Retest reminders, a clinician link, labs nearby and a lab order (US sandbox), each previewed and started by the person.</p>
  <p><b>Limits we state.</b> Data is encrypted at rest under a per-user key, but the server can unwrap it to run the agent; client-held keys are roadmap. Zero data retention terms are requested from the model provider, not confirmed.</p>
 </div></details>
</div></section>

<section id="traction"><div class="wrap">
 <h2>Measured numbers, and what we have not measured yet.</h2>
 <p class="lead">Pre-revenue, with no outside users yet, so no user numbers to claim.</p>
 <ul class="stats">
  <li class="stat"><b>1,825</b><span>tests in CI</span><small>Snapshot 11 Nov 2026, 0 failed</small></li><li class="stat"><b>16 s</b><span>median time per agent run</span><small>Range 13 to 59 s, 10 runs</small></li><li class="stat"><b>$0.052</b><span>model cost per run</span><small>6 runs, 13 Nov 2026</small></li><li class="stat"><b>1 tap</b><span>human in the loop</span><small>A person starts every run</small></li>
 </ul>
 <p class="note"><span class="ev h">Hypothesis</span><b>Not measured yet:</b> task success rate on real labs. It starts with the founder test. <b>A failure we fixed:</b> a model outage once looked like "no evidence"; now the screen says the result is incomplete and nothing is marked Cited.</p>
 <h3 style="margin-top:32px">Revenue model</h3>
 <ul class="grid g3">
  <li class="stat"><b>USD 199</b><span>a year</span><small>Locked for the first 100 members. A plan, not charged yet.</small></li><li class="stat"><b>~80%</b><span>gross margin</span><small>About USD 13 per member a month</small></li><li class="stat"><b>Later</b><span>partner labs, planned</span><small>Referral terms, ranked by evidence. No supplement sales.</small></li>
 </ul>
 <details><summary>Numbers and revenue model in full</summary><div>
  <p><b>Tests in CI.</b> Backend 1,476 and frontend 349 passing on main, 11 Nov 2026, 0 failed.</p>
  <p><b>Model cost per run.</b> Two model calls, measured on 6 runs on 13 Nov 2026.</p>
  <p><b>Human in the loop.</b> A person starts every run, plus one tap for every outside action.</p>
  <p><b>Not measured yet.</b> Task success rate on real labs: there are no real users and no labelled set yet. <b>A failure we fixed.</b> A model outage once looked like "no evidence"; now failed calls are counted, the screen says the result is incomplete, and nothing is marked Cited.</p>
  <p>The public demo runs on synthetic data. Pre-revenue, solo founder, self-funded.</p>
  <p><b>Founding price.</b> USD 199 a year, about USD 16.60 a month, locked for the first 100 members, billed on the web. A plan, not charged yet.</p>
  <p><b>Margin basis.</b> About 80% gross margin at the founding price, about USD 13 per member per month. Deliberately conservative; the measured agent cost uses a small part of it.</p>
  <p><b>Later.</b> Partner labs and tests on referral terms (planned), ranked by evidence, never by commission. No supplement sales. The Lab Agent as a pay-per-call tool for other agents is roadmap and not built. Users can already connect their own assistant to read their plan, with no lab values or marker names (beta).</p>
 </div></details>
</div></section>

<section id="founder"><div class="wrap two">
 <div><h2>Solo founder, with the gaps covered by design.</h2>
 <p class="lead">Paul Burg built the platform, the Lab Agent and the live demo alone. M.Sc. in environmental science, PhD coursework (ABD) in Sustainable Development, founder of his own ventures since 2011. <a class="tb" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/paul-burg" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a></p>
 <details><summary>How it was built, and the gaps in full</summary><div><p>Built with AI coding tools; every claim here is checked against the live app.</p><p><b>Gap: clinical.</b> No clinician on the team. Clinical markers go to Ask your clinician; no diagnoses, no doses. Seeking a clinical advisor.</p><p><b>Gap: security and legal.</b> Safety rules live in code, tests and logs, not promises. A data protection review comes before any EU or UAE users.</p></div></details></div>
 <ul class="rows" style="margin-top:0">
  <li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 3h6v6h6v6h-6v6H9v-6H3V9h6z"/></svg></span><div><h3>Gap: clinical</h3><p>No clinician on the team. Seeking a clinical advisor.</p></div></li><li><span class="sq"><svg class="ic" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l8 3v6c0 4.500-3.300 7.800-8 9-4.700-1.200-8-4.500-8-9V6z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/></svg></span><div><h3>Gap: security and legal</h3><p>A data protection review comes before any EU or UAE users.</p></div></li>
 </ul>
</div></section>

<section id="raise"><div class="wrap two">
 <div><h2>Three dated gates, then 100 founding members.</h2>
 <p class="lead">The beta is free. Each gate passes before the next opens; targets may change.</p>
 <div class="tile ask" style="margin-top:20px"><h3>The ask</h3><b>USD 500K post-money SAFE</b><p class="small" style="margin-top:8px">USD 5.5M cap, 15 months of runway, first close from USD 300K. Most of it goes to the team: an ML engineer, a data engineer and a data scientist. Pre-revenue and self-funded until now.</p></div></div>
 <ol class="gates" style="margin-top:0">
  <li><time datetime="2026-11-30">30 Nov 2026</time><p><b>Founder test on Paul's real labs.</b> At least 1 real lab through the agent.</p></li>
  <li><time datetime="2026-12-31">31 Dec 2026</time><p><b>5 friends test alone.</b> At least 3 of 5 finish a first run.</p></li>
  <li><time datetime="2027-01-31">31 Jan 2027</time><p><b>15 to 20 testers.</b> At least half finish a run; at least 3 upload a second lab.</p></li>
  <li><span>After the gates</span><p><b>100 founding slots</b> at USD 199 a year. We report 3-month retention.</p></li>
  <li><span>Mar to May 2027</span><p><b>Zero data retention confirmation</b> from the model provider; the Lab Agent as an MCP tool (roadmap).</p></li>
  <li><span>UAE</span><p><b>Partner pilot</b> with 1 or 2 labs or clinics after legal review. Beta users stay outside the EU and UAE until a data protection review.</p></li>
 </ol>
 <details style="grid-column:1/-1"><summary>Gates and funding in full</summary><div>
  <p><b>30 Nov 2026.</b> Founder test on Paul's real labs. At least 1 real lab through the agent; blockers triaged and wrong results fixed.</p>
  <p><b>31 Dec 2026.</b> 5 friends test alone. At least 3 of 5 finish a first run; usability findings logged.</p>
  <p><b>31 Jan 2027.</b> 15 to 20 testers, 3 coach talks. At least half finish a run; at least 3 upload a second lab.</p>
  <p>The beta is free. Each gate has to pass before the next one opens. Targets are proposed by the founder and may change.</p>
  <p><b>Funding and ask.</b> Raising USD 500K on a post-money SAFE with a USD 5.5M cap, for 15 months of runway; first close from USD 300K. Most of it goes to the team: an ML engineer, a data engineer and a data scientist. Pre-revenue and self-funded until now. Also: mentorship, UAE partners, and a hard review of our safety claims.</p>
 </div></details>
</div></section>

